[38;5;231m⏺[39m [1mDesign — Section 3: testing[0m

  [1mRunner:[0m [38;5;153mnode:test[39m with [38;5;153mnode:assert/strict[39m, invoked via [38;5;153mnpm test[39m → [38;5;153mnode --test test/[39m. No dependencies added;
  [38;5;153mpackage.json[39m gains only a [38;5;153mscripts.test[39m entry.

  [1mOne wrinkle worth naming, because it constrains file layout.[0m The validation modules are ES modules, but Node reads [38;5;153m.js
[39m  as CommonJS unless told otherwise — and [38;5;153msrc/index.js[39m / [38;5;153msrc/utils.js[39m are CommonJS that I'm not touching. So a root
  [38;5;153m"type": "module"[39m would break them. The fix is a one-line [38;5;153msrc/validation/package.json[39m containing [38;5;153m{"type":"module"}[39m,
  which marks just that directory as ESM. Browsers ignore it, Node respects it, and the unrelated [38;5;153msrc/[39m files keep
  working. Test files use the [38;5;153m.mjs[39m extension so they're ESM regardless of where they sit.

  [1mCoverage:[0m [38;5;153mrules.js[39m and [38;5;153mvalidate.js[39m get real unit tests — each rule's pass and fail cases plus its boundaries (empty
  string, whitespace-only, exact min/max length, range endpoints, a handful of valid and invalid emails), and for
  [38;5;153mvalidate[39m: first-failure-per-field ordering, clean input, multiple failing fields, unknown keys in [38;5;153mvalues[39m, and a schema
  key missing from [38;5;153mvalues[39m.

  [38;5;153mform.js[39m gets [1mno automated tests[0m — it needs a DOM, and you scoped out the Playwright/jsdom infrastructure that would
  provide one. That's a deliberate gap, not an oversight: the DOM contract (error node placement, clearing,
  [38;5;153maria-invalid[39m) will be verified by hand in the browser and stated as manually-verified. It's also the argument for
  keeping [38;5;153mform.js[39m thin — every piece of logic that lives in the tested core instead of the controller is a piece that
  doesn't depend on manual checking.

  [1mDevelopment follows TDD[0m for the core: tests for a rule before the rule.

